        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can use our knowledge of fraction multiplication to square fractions. </p>",
            "readable_text": "We can use our knowledge of fraction multiplication to square fractions.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, let&#x27;s evaluate the following squared fraction:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, let's evaluate the following squared fraction:\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we write <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left( \\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2]</span> with multiplication signs:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: ((3)/(5))^{2} = (3)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(5)_(\u23df)_([math]\\color{blue}2[/math] times)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we write [MATH: \\left( \\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2] with multiplication signs:\n[MATH: ((3)/(5))^{2} = (3)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(5)_(\u23df)_([math]\\color{blue}2[/math] times)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, we calculate the product of the two fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, we calculate the product of the two fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: ((3)/(5))^{2}|= (3)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(5); = (3 \u00d7 3)/(5 \u00d7 5); = (9)/(25)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: ((3)/(5))^{2}|= (3)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(5); = (3 \u00d7 3)/(5 \u00d7 5); = (9)/(25)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, we conclude that\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{9}{25}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, we conclude that\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{9}{25}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWe can use our knowledge of fraction multiplication to square fractions.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's evaluate the following squared fraction:\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2]\n\nContent:\nFirst, we write [MATH: \\left( \\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2] with multiplication signs:\n[MATH: ((3)/(5))^{2} = (3)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(5)_(\u23df)_([math]\\color{blue}2[/math] times)]\n\nContent:\nNow, we calculate the product of the two fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: ((3)/(5))^{2}|= (3)/(5) \u00d7 (3)/(5); = (3 \u00d7 3)/(5 \u00d7 5); = (9)/(25)]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we conclude that\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{9}{25}.]"
      },
