        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Find the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Find the value of [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We proceed in two steps:</p><ul><li><p>First, we write <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2]</span> with multiplication signs:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: ((4)/(5))^{2}|= (4)/(5) \u00d7 (4)/(5)_(\u23df)_([math]{\\color{blue}{2}}[/math] times)]</span></p></li><li><p>Then, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: ((4)/(5))^{2}|= (4)/(5) \u00d7 (4)/(5); = (4 \u00d7 4)/(5 \u00d7 5); = (16)/(25)]</span></p></li></ul><p>Therefore, we conclude that</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{16}{25}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We proceed in two steps:\n\n- First, we write [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2] with multiplication signs:\n[MATH: ((4)/(5))^{2}|= (4)/(5) \u00d7 (4)/(5)_(\u23df)_([math]{\\color{blue}{2}}[/math] times)]\n- Then, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n[MATH: ((4)/(5))^{2}|= (4)/(5) \u00d7 (4)/(5); = (4 \u00d7 4)/(5 \u00d7 5); = (16)/(25)]\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{16}{25}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe proceed in two steps:\n\n- First, we write [MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2] with multiplication signs:\n[MATH: ((4)/(5))^{2}|= (4)/(5) \u00d7 (4)/(5)_(\u23df)_([math]{\\color{blue}{2}}[/math] times)]\n- Then, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n[MATH: ((4)/(5))^{2}|= (4)/(5) \u00d7 (4)/(5); = (4 \u00d7 4)/(5 \u00d7 5); = (16)/(25)]\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n[MATH: \\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{16}{25}.]"
